@startuml admin-content-lifecycle
!theme plain
title A question's life — import to triage to soft delete (see docs/pyq/user-flows.md)

skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor<<student>> #E8F1FB
  BorderColor<<student>> #3A6EA5
}

state "DRAFT" as DRAFT
DRAFT : questions.status = DRAFT
DRAFT : invisible to students, visible in the admin list
DRAFT : edited at /admin/pyq/questions/{id}
DRAFT : 2-6 options, exactly one correct

state "PUBLISHED" as PUBLISHED
PUBLISHED : the only status GET pyq/questions and
PUBLISHED : POST pyq/sessions will draw from

state "Student sees it" as Seen <<student>>
Seen : answered, written to pyq.attempts
Seen : bookmarked or added to a collection

state "Report OPEN" as Reported <<student>>
Reported : pyq.question_reports.status = OPEN
Reported : shows in GET admin/pyq/questions?reported=true
Reported : and in the queue at /admin/pyq/reports

state "Report closed" as Closed
Closed : admin_note, resolved_by_id, resolved_at persisted
Closed : closing an already-closed report is a 409 — decided once
Closed : activity pyq.report_resolved / pyq.report_dismissed

state "Soft deleted" as Deleted
Deleted : questions.deleted_at set, the row stays
Deleted : hidden from students AND from admin lists
Deleted : past sessions, scores, reviews and reports still render it
Deleted : still blocks deleting its exam / subject / topic with a 409

[*] --> DRAFT : POST admin/pyq/questions/import\nupsert by external_key — the whole file is\nvalidated before anything is written
[*] --> DRAFT : POST admin/pyq/questions\n(Questions, New question)

DRAFT --> DRAFT : PATCH admin/pyq/questions/:id\noptions matched by id; one a student has already\nchosen can be reworded but not removed (409)
DRAFT --> PUBLISHED : PATCH .../status { PUBLISHED }\nactivity pyq.question_status_changed

PUBLISHED --> Seen : appears in the bank and in new sessions
Seen --> Reported : POST pyq/questions/:id/reports { reason, details }

Reported --> DRAFT : unpublish first if the question is wrong\nPATCH .../status { DRAFT }
Reported --> Closed : PATCH admin/pyq/reports/:id\n{ status: RESOLVED | DISMISSED, note? }
Closed --> PUBLISHED : question fixed and re-published

PUBLISHED --> DRAFT : PATCH .../status { DRAFT }\nunpublish — gone from new lists and sessions at once
PUBLISHED --> Deleted : DELETE admin/pyq/questions/:id
DRAFT --> Deleted : DELETE admin/pyq/questions/:id
Deleted --> [*]

note right of Deleted
  Soft, not hard, for two reasons: session_questions and
  attempts reference the question with onDelete: Restrict,
  and a student's old result should not change under them.
  For the same reason, correcting the right answer does not
  re-score attempts already made.
end note

note bottom of DRAFT
  Taxonomy (exams, subjects, topics) is managed separately at
  /admin/pyq/taxonomy: create, rename, reorder (PUT .../order
  with { slugs }). Slugs never change, and anything still
  referenced — even by a soft-deleted question — cannot be
  deleted (409).
end note

@enduml
